  {%- when 'RX 5700 XT' -%}
    <h2>RX 5700 XT at a glance</h2>
    <ul><li>Released: July 2019</li><li>Launch price: US$399 (the maker's price at launch, not today's shop price)</li><li>Video memory: 8 GB GDDR6</li><li>Power draw: about 225 watts</li><li>Power supply the maker recommends: 600 watts</li><li>Ray tracing hardware: no</li></ul>
    <p class="pc-checker__source">Specifications: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radeon_RX_5000_series" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikipedia</a>.</p>
    <h2>How the RX 5700 XT runs today's open-world games</h2>
    <p>GTA 6 has no PC version to test, so these are measured results from demanding open-world games that are already on PC. They are other people's tests, not ours, and they are not a prediction for GTA 6.</p>
    <div class="pc-checker__table-wrap"><table class="pc-checker__table pc-checker__table--compact"><thead><tr><th>Game</th><th>Resolution and settings</th><th>Average frames a second</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cyberpunk 2077</td><td>1920 x 1080, highest settings</td><td>58</td></tr><tr><td>Cyberpunk 2077</td><td>2560 x 1440, highest settings</td><td>37</td></tr><tr><td>Red Dead Redemption 2</td><td>1920 x 1080, highest settings</td><td>69</td></tr><tr><td>Red Dead Redemption 2</td><td>2560 x 1440, highest settings</td><td>56</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="pc-checker__source">Source: <a href="https://www.techpowerup.com/review/amd-radeon-rx-7600/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TechPowerUp</a> (May 2023).</p>
    <h2>Our take on the RX 5700 XT</h2>
    <p>The RX 5700 XT is one of the older cards that still clears our lowest level, 1080p with low settings. In the 2023 test above it averaged 58 frames a second in Cyberpunk 2077 at 1080p on the highest settings, so it has some room once settings come down. Its real weakness for a 2026 game is that it has no ray tracing hardware at all, so any lighting GTA 6 builds on ray tracing would have to be switched off or run in a slower fallback.</p>
    <h2>Upscaling and frame generation</h2>
    <p>The RX 5700 XT supports AMD's FSR 1, 2 and 3, including FSR 3 frame generation. It does not get AMD's newer machine-learning upscaler, which AMD lists for RX 6000 cards and newer.</p>
    <p>Whether GTA 6 on PC will include FSR has not been announced.</p>
    <h2>Against Rockstar's other PC games</h2>
    <p>Rockstar's most recent PC release is the 2025 enhanced version of GTA V. Its store page recommends an RTX 3060 or RX 6600 XT with 8 GB of video memory. On our own scoring the RX 5700 XT is about level with the RTX 3060.</p>
    <p>Red Dead Redemption 2, released on PC in 2019, recommends a GTX 1060 6GB. GTA 6 is a newer and much larger game than either, so expect its requirements to be higher than both.</p>
    <h2>Is there a laptop RX 5700 XT?</h2>
    <p>No laptop chip is sold under this exact name, so a laptop listed with a similar-sounding graphics chip is a different part. Check the exact model name in the checker below.</p>
