    <h2>Our take on the RTX 3050</h2>
    <p>The RTX 3050 is the slowest RTX card in our list and sits just above our lowest level. Its 8 GB of video memory is more than it can really use: in the 2023 test above it averaged 46 frames a second in Cyberpunk 2077 at 1080p and 28 at 1440p, so speed runs out before memory does. Expect 1080p, low settings and DLSS doing a lot of the work.</p>
    <h2>Upscaling and frame generation</h2>
    <p>The RTX 3050 supports DLSS Super Resolution, which draws the game at a lower resolution and sharpens it to your screen's resolution for more frames a second.</p>
    <p>It does not support DLSS Frame Generation, which needs an RTX 40 card or newer.</p>
    <p>Whether GTA 6 on PC will include DLSS has not been announced.</p>
    <h2>Against Rockstar's other PC games</h2>
    <p>Rockstar's most recent PC release is the 2025 enhanced version of GTA V. Its store page recommends an RTX 3060 or RX 6600 XT with 8 GB of video memory. On our own scoring the RTX 3050 is slower than the RTX 3060.</p>
    <p>Red Dead Redemption 2, released on PC in 2019, recommends a GTX 1060 6GB. GTA 6 is a newer and much larger game than either, so expect its requirements to be higher than both.</p>
    <h2>Is there a laptop RTX 3050?</h2>
    <p>Yes, a laptop chip is sold under the RTX 3050 name. It comes with 4 or 6 GB of video memory, where the desktop card has 8 GB, but it is a different, slower chip that runs at lower power, so do not read the desktop numbers on this page as laptop numbers.</p>
